  "notes": "Modified cash basis governmental funds (recorded as cash basis; fund balances equal cash, no liabilities); business-type Combined System Utilities Fund is accrual (net position measure). Governmental lines from the Total Governmental Funds column (p5). Beginning/ending cash = total fund balances 1,271,346 / 655,380 (cash 611,005 + county treasurer cash 44,375, p4). Transfers printed only as net (12,105) in the total column; gross: GF 595,016 in, Street 349,256 in, Sales Tax 564,549 out, Debt Service 363,828 out, Lottery 28,000 out, net 12,105 to the utility fund. Balance sheet: Statement of Net Position Total column (government-wide includes capital assets and debt, so not the fund balance sheet). Proprietary cash flow statement printed (p8: operating 473,811, noncapital 12,105, capital and related (154,003), investing 58, beginning cash 285,600, ending 617,571) but proprietary left null because report basis recorded as cash. Detail: General Fund from the department combining schedule (pp12-13), the more detailed schedule; the General Fund budgetary comparison (p9) is not recorded to avoid double counting. Street and Sales Tax budget schedules recorded; Street Motor vehicle and Bond proceeds lines have no actual and are omitted (budget 15,000 and 630,000). Debt Service and Lottery funds have no schedule. Read pages 1-13 of 13"
